Rule 1 (Input tensor 'a' must have at least one dimension.)
{a : tensor} |= ndim(a) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (The data type of tensor 'a' cannot be a string.)
{a : tensor} |= dtype_(a) ≠ "str"
>>
Rule 6 (Input tensor 'a' cannot be a boolean type.)
{a : tensor} |= dtype_(a) ≠ "bool"
>>
Rule 7 (The number of dimensions of input tensor 'a' must be less than or equal to 10.)
{a : tensor} |= ndim(a) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 8 (If the input tensor's dtype is complex, its minimum value's real part must be less than its maximum value's real part.)
{a : tensor} |= if dtype_(a) = "complex64" ∨ dtype_(a) = "complex128" then min(a) ≤ max(a)
>>
Rule 9 (If the input tensor's dtype is float, its min value must be less than its max value, or they have to be equal.)
{a : tensor} |= if dtype_(a) = "float16" ∨ dtype_(a) = "float32" ∨ dtype_(a) = "float64" then min(a) ≤ max(a)
>>
Rule 20 (If input tensor's dtype is int, its minimum value should be less than or equal to its max value)
{a : tensor} |= if dtype_(a) = "int" then min(a) ≤ max(a)
>>
Rule 21 (The dtype of the tensor 'a' should not be 'none'.)
{a : tensor} |= dtype_(a) ≠ "none"
>>
Rule 23 (The dimension of the tensor 'a' should be either 1, 2, or 3.)
{a: tensor} |= ndim(a) = 1 ∨ ndim(a) = 2 ∨ ndim(a) = 3
